{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le10ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le10ob02re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le10ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn9le10ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Kristi, thanks for agreeing to help me with my r\u00e9sum\u00e9. What I really need is to focus on writing an effective one. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Absolutely. What I really liked about the workshop is that the tips were really on point. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: For example?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: What a r\u00e9sum\u00e9 should do is help you land an interview. Once you get that, it will, hopefully, land you the job. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: I get it. What you said in the e-mail made sense. My r\u00e9sum\u00e9 is too general. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Right. The first thing we need to work on is the layout. What you want to present is a clearly organized summary of your qualifications. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: What a friend had told me is that a r\u00e9sum\u00e9 gets scanned for 25 seconds. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: And if your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 is hard to read and poorly organized, you won't even get an interview. <br />", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn9le10ob02re2img06.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: So, formatting, uh?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: To begin, use a logical format and wide margins. Do use clean type and clear headings. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Ok. I get it.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Then, you need to use bold and italic on areas that you want to catch the reader's eye. It is also important to use bullets to emphasize accomplishments.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: What you are saying is that I should identify accomplishments rather than just job descriptions. Right?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Yes! Include a one line job description and your list of accomplishments. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: And how do I go about doing that?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Use action verbs. Instead of saying you worked with customers, you could say you \u201ccemented relationships with customers\u201d. <br />", "id": 2, "time": "49000"}, {"image": "engenn9le10ob02re2img07.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: I like the sound of that. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: It says here you \u201chelped employees\u201d. You could rewrite this as you \u201cempowered employees through shared decisions\u201d. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Those are great. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: And don't write that you \u2018dealt with problems'... say \"I solved problems without increasing costs.\"<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Thanks, Kristi. You've been a great help. Let's grab a coffee. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Your treat?<br />", "id": 3, "time": "96000"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can exchange complex information about my work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can explain how to write a r\u00e9sum\u00e9.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about facts and courses of actions. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What does a r\u00e9sum\u00e9 look like? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What are some good things to have on your r\u00e9sum\u00e9?", "type":