4"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " What Clauses and Long Phrases as Subject", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use a <span class=\"italic\">what</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> that</span>, or<span class=\"italic\"> who </span> clause as the subject of a sentence, you have shifted the emphasis away from the words that sit in the subject position. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at these examples:<br> <span class=\"strong\">Original Sentence</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">The layout is the first thing we need to work on. </span> <br> (the emphasis here is on \u2018layout' because it's in the subject position) <br> <br> <span class=\"strong\">Noun Clause Sentence</span><br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What we need to work on first</span> is the layout. </span> <br> (the emphasis is now on \u2018what we need to work on' as it has been moved to the subject position) <br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "So, if you want to place emphasis on the verb, direct object, or another part of the sentence, you use a <span class=\"italic\">what-phrase</span> (or sometimes a <span class=\"italic\">that-clause</span>). ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">He really wanted to find a new job. </span><br>&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp  becomes<br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What he really wanted to find </span>was a new job. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This is how we form \u201cWhat\u201d clauses. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> subject / What-phrase</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" be \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">complement</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">The first thing we need to work on<br/> What you want to present<br/> What a friend had told me<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What you are saying </span></span> </div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is <br/> is<br/> is<br/>is</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">the layout.<br/> an organized summary of your qualifications. <br/> that a r\u00e9sum\u00e9 gets scanned for 25 seconds. <br/>I should identify accomplishments. </span> </div> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " R\u00e9sum\u00e9s & Action Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When writing a r\u00e9sum\u00e9, it is important to show your potential employer all your skills. In order for you to do that, you should use action verbs to help you describe these skills.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A good idea is to start your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 with bullet points that include action verbs. It will make your descriptions more powerful. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here are some action verbs you could use: <ul> <span class=\"italic\"><li>Instead of saying you worked with customers, you could say you \u201c<span class=\"strong\">cemented </span> relationship with customers\u201d</li> <li>It says here you \u201chelped employees\u201d. You could rewrite this as you \u201c<span class=\"strong\">empowered </span> employees through shared decisions\u201d. </li> <li>And don't write that you \u2018dealt with problems' ... say \u201cI <span class=\"strong\">solved </span> problems without increasing costs.\u201d</li> </span> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "More action verbs are listed below: <ul> <li>created, established, built, diagnosed, boosted, improved. </li> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember to use these verbs in the past. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Other important things to consider when writing your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 are: <ul><li>Format: use a chronological order as it allows you to highlight your experience.</li> <li>Margins: use wide margins </li> <li>Font: Clean type such as Times New Roman or Garamond. </li> <li>Headings: Clear and logical </li> <li>Other: Use<span class=\"strong\"> bold </span> and <span class=\"italic\">italic </span> on areas you want to catch the reader's eye. </li> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on point", "type": "name"}, {"content": "spot on or exactly right", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What I really liked about the workshop is that the tips were really on point. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about resumes.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "summary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a short account giving only the most important  information on something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We want to present a summary of your qualifications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to scan", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to read something very quickly in order to get the general idea ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A resume gets scanned for 25 seconds. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "margin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the space at the left or right side of a page where words are not written", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To begin, use wide margins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "format", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the appearance of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To begin, use a logical format.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to catch someone's eye", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get someone's attention", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to use bold and italic on areas that you want to catch the reader's eye. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bullet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a printed circle before each thing on a list so as to emphasize it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is also important to use bullets to emphasize accomplishments.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cement", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make an idea or relationship stronger", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I cemented relationships with customers. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to empower", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give someone more power to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I empowered employees through shared decisions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob02aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Reread the dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell a friend about 3 or 4 things you need to include on a r\u00e9sum\u00e9.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell your friend about your past academic or work related accomplishments.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write out a rough plan in bullet points of the information you would like to include in your own r\u00e9sum\u00e9.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss the plan with a friend.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I explain how to write a r\u00e9sum\u00e9.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I exchange complex information about my work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about complex information about my work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my information with someone.", "type": "text"}]}]}